<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.weather.dashboard_render</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/xiong/weather/scripts/dashboard_render_sweep.sh</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/xiong/weather</string>
  <!-- Thirty minutes, which is the cadence the section cache was written
       against: its nine lifetimes run 150 to 270 minutes and are staggered
       so that no single render expires the whole set.

       The render used to be scheduled inside the resident, on its own
       executor, with a 2400s timeout attached.  That timeout was the reason
       the page went stale: a render that needs longer is SIGTERMed before it
       writes, and it writes nothing at all; measured 2026-09-09, a run
       that started 09:24:29Z was killed at 2408s having produced no file,
       and the page still carried a build from 07:52Z.  It is also self-
       reinforcing: a killed render refreshes no cached section, so the next
       one starts colder and is killed sooner in its own work.  The last
       render that completed reused nine of twenty-one sections and took
       678s; the ones being killed were computing all of them.

       A render is a reader.  It takes no write lock, nothing waits on it,
       and there is no deadline it can miss that killing it does not miss
       worse.  launchd imposes no timeout, and the script's own
       single_instance guard is what keeps a slow render from stacking:
       a start that arrives while one is running exits 0 having skipped. -->
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>1800</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <!-- The kill left no trace anywhere on 2026-09-09: the resident recorded
       timeout_killed in a status field nothing on the page reads, and the
       render itself had no log of its own. -->
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/xiong/weather/data/logs/dashboard_render.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/xiong/weather/data/logs/dashboard_render.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
